 "key_findings": [
  "J2-lenient mean is 0.248 higher than J1-strict overall — lenient judge inflates scores across the board",
  "B-nofreeze: J1 .111 vs J2 .906 (diff -0.795) — biggest divergence; J2 essentially gives nofreeze near-full marks while J1 says it failed",
  "A-full and B-2del-eo: J2 = 1.000 flat (ceiling effect) — lenient judge cannot distinguish good configs",
  "consequence: any single-judge analysis using J2 alone would conclude \"nofreeze barely matters\" (diff A-B ~0.09), contradicting J1-based main analysis (diff ~0.82); judge choice flips the headline finding",
  "this is a concrete instance of the R5 family_check concern: two judges from the same model family (both Qwen-family per calibration design) disagree by up to 1.0 on individual runs; κ between them at run-level binary pass/fail needs computation before seedc judging"
